    "created_at": "2022-03-10T17:16:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-10T17:16:01Z",
    "body": "The issue I talk about is not about lacking semantics, but just about the fact that copy-pasting from an HTML document typically takes the raw text contents, which loses semantics by its very nature.  I don't think we need to add anything to HTML to address this.\r\n\r\nIn particular, adding `<exponent>` would be one tiny patch on a much larger spread of formatting; you get the same issues (luckily less prone to misinterpretation) when CO<sub>2</sub> is copy-pasted as CO2, when matrix indexes get linearized, etc. To the extent that math markup could use better structural/semantic support, we already have MathML in the platform. 10<sup>6</sup> could, if desired, be written as `<math><apply><power/><cn>10</cn><cn>6</cn></apply></math>`, or `<math><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>` with all the semantics you could desire *and* an existing layout model.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
